From: sheng-development
Subject: [PATCH] Broadcast sensor availability instead of only telling claimants

send_dbus_event() builds its recipient list from data->clients[], so a
PropertiesChanged for HasAccelerometer only ever reaches clients that
already hold a claim. Upstream that is harmless: find_sensors() is a sysfs
scan, so the property is already correct before anything connects.

With the SSC drivers it is not. libssc waits 5s for the QRTR bus in every
discover(), and there are four of them, so HasAccelerometer stays false for
about 20s after the bus name is taken. KWin latches onto the service the
moment it registers, reads HasAccelerometer once, gets false, and never
hears otherwise -- it never claims the accelerometer, so it is not in
data->clients[]. The output keeps Capability::AutoRotation unset and Plasma
offers no auto-rotate control (kscreen-doctor: "Auto Rotate Policy:
incapable").

Availability is not private to claimants. Broadcast it, both when a driver
appears or disappears and once discovery has finished. Readings stay
directed at the clients that asked for them.
--- a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
+++ b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
@@ -240,7 +240,7 @@
 	GVariantBuilder props_builder;
 	GVariant *props_changed = NULL;
 
-	g_return_if_fail (destination_bus_name != NULL);
+	/* A NULL destination broadcasts */
 
 	g_variant_builder_init (&props_builder, G_VARIANT_TYPE ("a{sv}"));
 
@@ -377,16 +377,21 @@
 send_driver_changed_dbus_event (SensorData   *data,
 				DriverType    driver_type)
 {
+	PropertiesMask mask;
+
 	if (driver_type == DRIVER_TYPE_ACCEL)
-		send_dbus_event (data, PROP_HAS_ACCELEROMETER);
+		mask = PROP_HAS_ACCELEROMETER;
 	else if (driver_type == DRIVER_TYPE_LIGHT)
-		send_dbus_event (data, PROP_HAS_AMBIENT_LIGHT);
+		mask = PROP_HAS_AMBIENT_LIGHT;
 	else if (driver_type == DRIVER_TYPE_PROXIMITY)
-		send_dbus_event (data, PROP_HAS_PROXIMITY);
+		mask = PROP_HAS_PROXIMITY;
 	else if (driver_type == DRIVER_TYPE_COMPASS)
-		send_dbus_event (data, PROP_HAS_COMPASS);
+		mask = PROP_HAS_COMPASS;
 	else
 		g_assert_not_reached ();
+
+	/* KWin reads HasAccelerometer without ever claiming the sensor */
+	send_dbus_event_for_client (data, NULL, mask);
 }
 
 static gboolean
@@ -782,8 +787,10 @@
 	if (!any_sensors_left (data))
 		goto bail;
 
-	send_dbus_event (data, PROP_ALL);
-	send_dbus_event (data, PROP_ALL_COMPASS);
+	/* Clients that read the properties during the SSC discovery wait saw
+	 * every sensor as absent, and no claim means no directed signal. */
+	send_dbus_event_for_client (data, NULL, PROP_ALL);
+	send_dbus_event_for_client (data, NULL, PROP_ALL_COMPASS);
 	return;
 
 bail:
